  "body": "**What.** After #82 ends, run a short stretch of #82's own path twice on win2 and compare: `amp_flint_par.py` at \u03c9/\u03c9\u221e = 1.10, K 45, J 1500, 1280 bits, stopped at k 20. Recommended by win2 in #146's summary.\n\n**Why.** #146 covered lemma 6a(5) and the K 15, 640-bit amplitude path, not #82's K 45, 1280-bit one, where the night's faults hit (#82's 1.10 worker). Two runs that agree bit for bit to k 20 on that path add to #147's cross-check against the K 33 runs.\n\n**Acceptance (can fail).** The two logs agree at every order to k 20 (`log_compare.py`), or the first difference is named. #82's own 1.10 log is the third comparand.\n\n**Depends on.** #82.\n",
